       :logos {:title "Logos and credits"
               :html "<h2>Logos</h2>\n<p><strong>1. La Biennale di Venezia, 61st International Art Exhibition, National Participations</strong> (&quot;61. Esposizione Internazionale d&#39;Arte / Partecipazioni Nazionali&quot;)</p>\n<p>Required on the press release and on all printed and digital materials about the Pavilion. Versions:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Colour (main version):</strong> Pantone 186 C · CMYK 0 / 91 / 76 / 6 · RGB 205 / 0 / 30</li>\n<li><strong>Black (subsidiary):</strong> for one-colour black printing</li>\n<li><strong>Negative (subsidiary):</strong> white outline version for dark backgrounds</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Rules from La Biennale&#39;s logo guide (2026):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Minimum width 25 mm (0.98 in).</li>\n<li>Place it at the top right. On a vertical page the top margin is 1/16 of the page height and the logo is 1/8 of the height tall; on a square page 1/12 and 1/6; on a horizontal page 1/10 and 1/5; on a page more than twice as wide as it is tall, 1/6 and 1/3. The right margin equals the width of the logo&#39;s vertical bar.</li>\n<li>Only institutional logos may sit in the header. Commercial and sponsor logos go in the footer.</li>\n<li>Do not change the logo&#39;s colours or shape or the lion silhouette, and do not stretch or distort it.</li>\n<li>Avoid backgrounds that weaken the logo; on photographs or coloured fields, use the red, black or negative version, whichever reads clearly.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>2. The Studio</strong> square logo (PNG, vector PDF and EPS)</p>\n<h2>Image credits</h2>\n<p>Every image in the press kit comes with its own caption. Please print it as given. Captions follow La Biennale&#39;s style: the work&#39;s title in italics, entries separated by full stops, several names under one entry separated by semicolons, the artist called &quot;the Artist&quot; in the credit, and no full stop at the end.</p>\n<p><strong>Pavilion</strong> (installation views)</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Zadik Zadikian, <em>Big Red Bed Where Dreams Come True</em>, 2026. Plaster, acrylic, pure pigment and EPS foam. Installation view, <em>Zadik Zadikian: The Studio</em>, Armenian Pavilion, Biennale Arte 2026. Photo Aram Zadikian. Courtesy the Artist; Zadik Zadikian Studio</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Process</strong> (work in progress in Tesa 41)</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Zadik Zadikian painting the green of the Italian flag, Tesa 41, Arsenale, October 2026. <em>Zadik Zadikian: The Studio</em>, Armenian Pavilion, Biennale Arte 2026. Photo Aram Zadikian. Courtesy Zadik Zadikian Studio</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Renderings</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Zadik Zadikian, <em>7 Steps to Heaven</em>, 2026. Plaster, pure pigment and acrylic. Rendering of the proposed work in Tesa 41. Rendering Aram Zadikian. Courtesy the Artist; Zadik Zadikian Studio</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>People</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Zadik Zadikian and Tony Shafrazi in Tesa 41, Armenian Pavilion, Biennale Arte 2026. Photo Aram Zadikian. Courtesy Zadik Zadikian Studio</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Archive</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Zadik Zadikian, <em>Gold Bricks</em>, 1978. Plaster and 24-karat gold leaf. Installation view, Tony Shafrazi Gallery, Tehran, 1978. Photographer unknown. Courtesy the Artist</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Video</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><em>Seven Steps to Heaven</em>, 2026. Video, colour, sound, 2:26. Filmed in Tesa 41, Arsenale, October 2026. Camera [name]; editing [name]. Courtesy Zadik Zadikian Studio</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2>Terms of use</h2>\n<p>Images and video are supplied for editorial use in connection with <em>Zadik Zadikian: The Studio</em> only. Please do not crop into the work, alter colours or add text, and always print the full credit.</p>\n"
               :text "Logos\n\n1. La Biennale di Venezia, 61st International Art Exhibition, National Participations (\"61. Esposizione Internazionale d'Arte / Partecipazioni Nazionali\")\n\nRequired on the press release and on all printed and digital materials about the Pavilion. Versions:\n\n- Colour (main version): Pantone 186 C · CMYK 0 / 91 / 76 / 6 · RGB 205 / 0 / 30\n- Black (subsidiary): for one-colour black printing\n- Negative (subsidiary): white outline version for dark backgrounds\n\nRules from La Biennale's logo guide (2026):\n\n- Minimum width 25 mm (0.98 in).\n- Place it at the top right. On a vertical page the top margin is 1/16 of the page height and the logo is 1/8 of the height tall; on a square page 1/12 and 1/6; on a horizontal page 1/10 and 1/5; on a page more than twice as wide as it is tall, 1/6 and 1/3. The right margin equals the width of the logo's vertical bar.\n- Only institutional logos may sit in the header. Commercial and sponsor logos go in the footer.\n- Do not change the logo's colours or shape or the lion silhouette, and do not stretch or distort it.\n- Avoid backgrounds that weaken the logo; on photographs or coloured fields, use the red, black or negative version, whichever reads clearly.\n\n2. The Studio square logo (PNG, vector PDF and EPS)\n\nImage credits\n\nEvery image in the press kit comes with its own caption. Please print it as given. Captions follow La Biennale's style: the work's title in italics, entries separated by full stops, several names under one entry separated by semicolons, the artist called \"the Artist\" in the credit, and no full stop at the end.\n\nPavilion (installation views)\n> Zadik Zadikian, Big Red Bed Where Dreams Come True, 2026. Plaster, acrylic, pure pigment and EPS foam. Installation view, Zadik Zadikian: The Studio, Armenian Pavilion, Biennale Arte 2026. Photo Aram Zadikian. Courtesy the Artist; Zadik Zadikian Studio\n\nProcess (work in progress in Tesa 41)\n> Zadik Zadikian painting the green of the Italian flag, Tesa 41, Arsenale, October 2026. Zadik Zadikian: The Studio, Armenian Pavilion, Biennale Arte 2026. Photo Aram Zadikian. Courtesy Zadik Zadikian Studio\n\nRenderings\n> Zadik Zadikian, 7 Steps to Heaven, 2026. Plaster, pure pigment and acrylic. Rendering of the proposed work in Tesa 41. Rendering Aram Zadikian. Courtesy the Artist; Zadik Zadikian Studio\n\nPeople\n> Zadik Zadikian and Tony Shafrazi in Tesa 41, Armenian Pavilion, Biennale Arte 2026. Photo Aram Zadikian. Courtesy Zadik Zadikian Studio\n\nArchive\n> Zadik Zadikian, Gold Bricks, 1978. Plaster and 24-karat gold leaf. Installation view, Tony Shafrazi Gallery, Tehran, 1978. Photographer unknown. Courtesy the Artist\n\nVideo\n> Seven Steps to Heaven, 2026. Video, colour, sound, 2:26. Filmed in Tesa 41, Arsenale, October 2026. Camera [name]; editing [name]. Courtesy Zadik Zadikian Studio\n\nTerms of use\n\nImages and video are supplied for editorial use in connection with Zadik Zadikian: The Studio only. Please do not crop into the work, alter colours or add text, and always print the full credit."
