       :video {:title nil
               :films [{:slug "seven-steps-to-heaven"
                        :held false
                        :title "Seven Steps to Heaven"
                        :date "October 2026"
                        :credit "Film: Aram Zadikian. Courtesy Zadik Zadikian Studio"
                        :line "A stair of seven steps that goes nowhere, carried by hand into Tesa 41 and painted white: on cubes, journeys, the present, and a climb to heaven in a small space."
                        :html "<p>The studio team unloads the white sections of a seven-step stair and carries them through the Arsenale into Tesa 41. Zadik Zadikian measures and places them against the corner of two walls, and the team fills and paints them white. Assistants talk about cubes, journeys and the present, and about a stair that leads nowhere. English subtitles are burned in.</p>\n"}
                       {:slug "italian-flag"
                        :held false
                        :title "The Italian Flag"
                        :date "October 2026"
                        :credit "Film: Aram Zadikian. Courtesy Zadik Zadikian Studio"
                        :line "Zadik Zadikian and the studio paint and build an Italian flag from separate green, white and red units that stand on their own feet."
                        :html "<p>In Tesa 41, Zadik Zadikian and assistants spread green and red paint over large white panels, then build the flag from units that two people can lift, carry and set upright. Between the work, Zadikian talks with Aram Zadikian and with visitors about where the idea came from and about blocks of colour. English subtitles are burned in.</p>\n"}
                       {:slug "carrying"
                        :held false
                        :title "Carrying"
                        :date "October 2026"
                        :credit "Film: Aram Zadikian. Courtesy Zadik Zadikian Studio"
                        :line "Aram Zadikian carries a tall red unit on his back from Tesa 41 through the Arsenale and the streets of Castello, and back."
                        :html "<p>Aram Zadikian straps a tall red unit to a backpack frame in Tesa 41 and walks it out of the pavilion. He crosses the wooden bridge at the Arsenale gate, passes the stone lions and goes on through the streets of Castello, stopping to talk on the way. Zadik Zadikian walks with him. The film ends back in the studio.</p>\n"}
                       {:slug "murano"
                        :held false
                        :title "Murano"
                        :date "October 2026"
                        :credit "Film: Aram Zadikian. Courtesy Zadik Zadikian Studio"
                        :line "A visit to a glass furnace on Murano, and a conversation at lunch about glass, artists and the people who make it."
                        :html "<p>Glassblowers shape a dark glass piece at the furnace while Zadik Zadikian and his guests watch. At a table outside, two men talk about glass as a material, about shopkeepers and artists, and about glass made to be collected. The film ends back in Tesa 41, where the team paints and moves flag units. English subtitles are burned in.</p>\n"}
                       {:slug "before-the-flag"
                        :held false
                        :title "Before the Flag"
                        :date "September 2026"
                        :credit "Film: Aram Zadikian. Courtesy Zadik Zadikian Studio"
                        :line "Zadik and Aram Zadikian talk over a white model in Tesa 41: heights, roofs and the city."
                        :html "<p>In Tesa 41, Zadik Zadikian and Aram Zadikian stand on either side of a white foam model with a stepped, notched top. They talk about heights, about the feeling of standing on a roof in the city, and about what the shape brings to mind. Shots of the lagoon follow. English subtitles are burned in.</p>\n"}
                       {:slug "tesa-41-september"
                        :held true
                        :title "In Tesa 41"
                        :date "September 2026"
                        :credit "Film: Aram Zadikian. Courtesy Zadik Zadikian Studio"
                        :line "A working day in Tesa 41: fitting white units together, mixing pigment and casting, and deliveries brought in by hand."
                        :html "<p>Tall white units are fitted together on the floor of Tesa 41. Assistants pour pigment, cast and check small units at the workbench, and a parcel comes up a bridge on a hand trolley. Boats pass on a Venetian canal. Zadik Zadikian stands beside a piece and explains it. The film closes on the studio&#39;s title card.</p>\n"}
                       {:slug "maquette"
                        :held false
                        :title "The Maquette"
                        :date "February 2026"
                        :credit "Film: Aram Zadikian. Courtesy Zadik Zadikian Studio"
                        :line "Zadik Zadikian works out a full-size maquette in white foam at a foam-cutting plant, months before Venice."
                        :html "<p>The film opens on a 3D model on screen, pink units and gilded bricks. In a foam-cutting plant, Zadik Zadikian sets out large white blocks, adds small steps and feet, checks proportions on his phone and explains the forms to camera. Cutting machines and stacks of foam fill the background.</p>\n"}
                       {:slug "leaning-red"
                        :held false
                        :title "Leaning Red"
                        :date "February 2026"
                        :credit "Film: Aram Zadikian. Courtesy Zadik Zadikian Studio"
                        :line "Zadik Zadikian and two helpers build a full-size cardboard mock-up of Leaning Red and stand it against a wall."
                        :html "<p>Outdoors, Zadik Zadikian measures, cuts and tapes sheets of honeycomb cardboard into a tall slab with two helpers. The mock-up is carried inside and leaned against a wall to check its height and angle, with a narrow blue unit beside it. There is no speech; the soundtrack is music only.</p>\n"}]}}
